# SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
# The view's memory stays bounded while a sketch preview follows the
# pointer (mitcad#2452, mitcad#2485; the cause and fix in mitcad#2437).
# Each sketch overlay picture is a view-sized texture that OCCT lets go
# only at full frames; on Apple silicon graphics memory counts in the
# process footprint, which the memory guard compares with installed RAM.
#   1. Center Point Arc after the reported sequence (Midpoint Line,
#      Centerline, Line, Centerline twice): the radius preview, then the
#      sweep preview, follow the pointer; the arc commits.
#   2. A typed radius, the sweep following the pointer.
#   3. Sketch Dimension on each arc of a two-arc profile (GitHub #681's
#      shape): the value follows the pointer, then the radius commits.
# Each preview may grow the footprint by at most 400 MB: a few replaced
# pictures, where every move once kept one (19 MB at 1440 x 838 points
# on a 2x screen). Run by tools/ui-macos-sketch-preview-memory-test.sh.
expect-ever 'View area'
sleep 800
command sketch.create
click-logged 'Datum xy'
expect-log 'Sketch started on xy'
wait-idle

# The reported sequence before Center Point Arc.
command sketch.line_midpoint
sketch-click 0 40
sketch-click 30 40
key Escape
command sketch.centerline
command sketch.line
sketch-click -60 60
sketch-click 60 60
key Escape
command sketch.centerline
command sketch.centerline
wait-idle

# 1. Center Point Arc: the radius preview follows the pointer.
